in deep chain a design requires a  three-dimensional protein complex  structure  either experimentally resolved or  modeled computationally  deep chain currently supports protein  data bank format for these  and you can either upload one using a  local file or simply type in the four  character code  of a pdb structure from a design you  will be able to explore protein  sequences  in the playground run molecular dynamics  simulations  or use the ai designer to conduct  mutagenesis experiments  let's create one now in the new design  tab  enter your design name for me it will be  defensin  and select your data source in this case  it will be a local file  describing a defense in six complex  using a local file is the default option  and there it is i can visualize my  structure on the left  and start working on it now for a given  project  you might be interested in not one but  several complexes that your protein of  interest forms  perhaps an example from a different  species or a structure of a mutant  for my defensing project i found one in  a pdb file  that i would like to analyze more  closely  it is a structure of a variant where h  histidine 27  was mutated to w tryptophan which made  it unable to block  invasions i can create another design in  deep chain from this complex just by  using the 4 character pdb id  all i need to do here is to create a new  design let's call it simply defense  invariant here  select four character pdb id as a data  source  enter my code 3 q t  e and hit create design  finally i realized that my first design  was not appropriately named  i can rename it by going to the upper  section of the screen  where my active design is displayed and  rename it there  there it is we've seen how to create  designs both from a local file  or from the rcsb pdb and how to rename  them  thanks so much for your attention and  enjoy deep chain
 

